ers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmcdo29/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmcdo29/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmcdo29/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmcdo29/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmcdo29/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmcdo29/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmcdo29/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmcdo29/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-02-26T20:52:47Z","updated_at":"2021-02-26T20:52:47Z","body":"You're still able to now pass a custom class to the `ClientsModule` and do some extension of the `ClientGrpc` class. When implementing this, I was not aware that `Grpc` has some different methods to it.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nestjs/nest/issues/comments/786888124/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nestjs/nest/issues/comments/787847729","html_url":"https://github.com/nestjs/nest/pull/5710#issuecomment-787847729","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nestjs/nest/issues/5710","id":787847729,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDc4Nzg0NzcyOQ==","user":{"login":"kamilmysliwiec","id":23244943,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMjQ0OTQz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23244943?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kamilmysliwiec","html_url":"https://github.com/kamilmysliwiec","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kamilmysliwiec/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kamilmysliwiec/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kamilmysliwiec/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kamilmysliwiec/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kamilmysliwiec/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kamilmysliwiec/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kamilmysliwiec/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kamilmysliwiec/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kamilmysliwiec/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-03-01T10:44:04Z","updated_at":"2021-03-01T10:44:04Z","body":"gRPC transport strategy does not require any specific mapping of successful/error responses and so neither of these methods is called. @ssilve1989 in this case, I'd suggest registering a custom exception filter instead.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nestjs/nest/issues/comments/787847729/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nestjs/nest/issues/comments/788069319","html_url":"https://github.com/nestjs/nest/pull/5710#issuecomment-788069319","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nestjs/nest/issues/5710","id":788069319,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDc4ODA2OTMxOQ==","user":{"login":"ssilve1989","id":3699455,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2OTk0NTU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3699455?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ssilve1989","html_url":"https://github.com/ssilve1989","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ssilve1989/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ssilve1989/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ssilve1989/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ssilve1989/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ssilve1989/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ssilve1989/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ssilve1989/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ssilve1989/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ssilve1989/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-03-01T16:08:38Z","updated_at":"2021-03-01T16:08:38Z","body":"@kamilmysliwiec I don't think that is sufficient. \r\n\r\nGiven an example where there are 3 parties involved\r\n\r\n- external gRPC Client (BloomRPC, gRPC Curl, gRPC service etc)\r\n- a gRPC service (service A)\r\n- a gRPC service (service B)\r\n\r\nWhen the client makes a request as \r\n - client -> serviceA -> serviceB\r\n\r\nand serviceB throws a gRPC error conforming to the grpc status object. This will be properly logged in `serviceA` from the built in `RpcExceptionsHandler` however, at that point, it will propagate back up to the client as `Error: 2 UNKNOWN: Internal server error` losing any information that was provided by `serviceB` such as status codes and descriptions.\r\n\r\nI believe this is because the `ClientGrpc` receives an error and just throws it. It does not match `@Catch(RpcException)` or the whatever custom filter you make, but rather requires `@Catch()` which leaves it up to the filter to determine if this was a gRPC error or not by doing something like inspecting its properties.\r\n\r\nI verified this by printing the `exception.constructor.name` in a custom exception filter with `@Catch()` and can see that in serviceA it logs `Error` instead of any custom exception. This would be remedied if the ClientGrpc could utilize `deserializeError` and transform it into my custom exception","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nestjs/nest/issues/comments/788069319/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nestjs/nest/issues/comments/850318731","html_url":"https://github.com/nestjs/nest/pull/5710#issuecomment-850318731","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nestjs/nest/issues/5710","id":850318731,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDg1MDMxODczMQ==","user":{"login":"MickL","id":5103210,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMDMyMTA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5103210?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MickL","html_url":"https://github.com/MickL","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MickL/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MickL/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MickL/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MickL/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MickL/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MickL/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MickL/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MickL/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MickL/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-05-28T10:25:03Z","updated_at":"2021-05-28T10:25:38Z","body":"@kamilmysliwiec \r\n\r\nI am refering to https://github.com/nestjs/nest/issues/6496 but conversation was locked. I am not sure how this PR is related to what I described in #6496 :\r\n\r\nService A calls Service B -> Service B microservice controller throws normal `Error` \"hello world\" -> Service A logs \"ERROR [WsExceptionsHandler] Internal server error\" instead of \"hello world\".\r\n\r\nI would expect a microservice controller to catch all unrecognized exceptions (not RpcException) and make an RpcException so Service A actually logs \"hello world\".\r\n\r\nFor http controllers thats exactly the case: It catches all unrecognized errors (not HttpException) and makes them an HttpException.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nestjs/nest/issues/comments/850318731/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]